  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "People carry one or two given names and up to four family names, with the mother's family names first and the father's last (Ana Sofia Pereira Martins). People go by their last family name (Martins), sometimes the last two. Given names must come from an official list, so traditional names dominate: João, Maria, Francisco, Leonor. Particles like da, dos and de are common (Joana dos Santos). Lisbon and Porto have large Brazilian communities, Cape Verdeans and Angolans with long roots in Lisbon, and newer Nepali, Indian, Bangladeshi and Ukrainian communities.",
